**user**:
> I'm using Shiny and now (I'm not sure what changed), by pickerInputs won't open. They show the default, but nothing happens when I click on them. I don't see any javascript errors in the console when I do this.
**assistant**:
> Let’s triage this step by step. This kind of “pickerInput won’t open, no JS error” usually comes down to one of a few things:
> 
> 1. **Missing / not loaded `shinyWidgets` JS/CSS**
> 2. **Version mismatch (shiny vs shinyWidgets vs bootstrap)**
> 3. **CSS/JS conflict (e.g., overlay blocking clicks, bootstrap 5 vs 3, etc.)**
> 4. **UI created before `shinyWidgets` is attached (rare but possible with modules / HTML templates)**
> 
> I’ll give you a minimal diagnostic checklist and a tiny reproducible test. If that test works, we know it’s something in your app; if not, it’s a package / environment issue.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 1. Quick minimal test
> 
> Create a *new* file `picker_test.R` with nothing else loaded and run it:
> 
> ```r
> library(shiny)
> library(shinyWidgets)
> 
> ui <- fluidPage(
>   titlePanel("pickerInput test"),
>   sidebarLayout(
>     sidebarPanel(
>       pickerInput(
>         inputId = "test_picker",
>         label = "Choose a letter",
>         choices = LETTERS[1:5],
>         options = list(`live-search` = TRUE)
>       )
>     ),
>     mainPanel(
>       verbatimTextOutput("sel")
>     )
>   )
> )
> 
> server <- function(input, output, session) {
>   output$sel <- renderPrint(input$test_picker)
> }
> 
> shinyApp(ui, server)
> ```
> 
> Tell me what happens in that app:
> 
> - If **the dropdown opens and works**, then the core stack is fine and something in your main app is interfering.
> - If **the dropdown still doesn’t open**, it’s almost certainly a version/load issue; go to section 2.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 2. Check versions and conflicts
> 
> In an R console (not inside a Shiny session):
> 
> ```r
> sessionInfo()
> packageVersion("shiny")
> packageVersion("shinyWidgets")
> ```
> 
> Useful checks:
> 
> - `shinyWidgets` should be reasonably recent relative to `shiny`. Big gaps can break JS.
> - If you’ve recently switched to **bslib / Bootstrap 5**, older shinyWidgets versions can misbehave.
> 
> If you see something like:
> 
> ```r
> other attached packages:
> [1] bslib_0.7.0 ... shinyWidgets_0.7.6 ... shiny_1.9.0
> ```
> 
> then it’s worth updating everything:
> 
> ```r
> update.packages(ask = FALSE, checkBuilt = TRUE)
> # or minimally:
> install.packages("shinyWidgets")
> install.packages("shiny")
> install.packages("bslib")
> ```
> 
> Then re-run the minimal test app.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 3. Check JS/CSS actually loaded
> 
> In your *broken* app, open the browser dev tools (F12):
> 
> 1. Go to **Network** tab, filter by `picker` or by “JS”.
> 2. Reload the app.
> 3. You should see something like `shinyWidgets-bindings.js` (name varies by version) being loaded, plus the associated CSS.
> 
> If those files aren’t being loaded:
> 
> - Confirm that you have `library(shinyWidgets)` in the **global scope**, not just inside `server` or inside a module.
> - Make sure you don’t have a custom HTML template that omits `htmlDependency`s from R.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 4. Inspect the element & see if something blocks clicks
> 
> Sometimes the pickerInput is “working” but a CSS overlay div is catching clicks, so there’s no JS error but nothing opens.
> 
> In the dev tools:
> 
> 1. Right-click on the picker input → “Inspect”.
> 2. Look at the HTML; normally you see something like:
> 
>    ```html
>    <div class="form-group shiny-input-container">
>      <label ...>Choose a letter</label>
>      <div class="bs-select ...">
>        <button type="button" class="btn dropdown-toggle ...">...</button>
>        ...
>    ```
> 
> 3. Move your mouse around and watch the layout inspector: is some full-page `<div>` (modal overlay, loading screen, etc.) sitting **above** it?
> 
> If so, check:
> 
> - Any custom CSS like:
> 
>   ```css
>   .some-overlay {
>     position: fixed;
>     top: 0; left: 0;
>     width: 100%; height: 100%;
>     z-index: 9999;
>   }
>   ```
> 
>   without being hidden/removed.
> 
> - Any UI elements from packages like `waiter`, `shinybusy`, etc., that might stay active.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 5. Common recent-breaking-changes causes
> 
> A few specific things you may have recently changed:
> 
> 1. **Switched to `bslib::bs_theme()` or to `theme = bslib::bs_theme(version = 5)`**  
>    Some older shinyWidgets versions weren’t fully compatible with bootstrap 5. Updating `shinyWidgets` usually fixes it.
> 
> 2. **Start using `navbarPage()` with `theme` and custom JS**  
>    If you load custom Bootstrap JS or CSS after shiny’s own dependencies, you can override the dropdown behavior. Search your code for `<script src=...bootstrap...>` or `<link href=...bootstrap...>` and try temporarily removing them.
> 
> 3. **Moved `library(shinyWidgets)` into `server` or a module**  
>    That prevents Shiny from registering the input binding for `pickerInput`. Make sure it’s at top-level.
> 
> ---
> 
